# Gulf Mover — environment variables (example only; copy to .env for local runs)
#
# SECURITY: every VITE_* variable below is embedded into the browser bundle by
# Vite. Only PUBLIC values may ever be placed here. The Supabase service_role
# (secret) key must never be stored in this file, a .env file, or anywhere the
# browser can read. RLS policies are what limit the publishable key's power.

# Application mode. Leave unset (or anything other than "production") to run
# the existing localStorage demo exactly as before. Set to "production" to
# require and use the Supabase configuration below (missing/invalid setup then
# produces a clear configuration error instead of silent demo fallback).
VITE_APP_MODE=demo

# Supabase project settings — required ONLY when VITE_APP_MODE=production.
# Placeholder values are not real credentials.
#
# SERVER-KEY SAFEGUARD: keys beginning with "sb_secret_" (or legacy JWTs whose
# payload role is "service_role") are rejected by the configuration validator.
# This is a best-effort safeguard, NOT a guarantee — treat VITE_* as
# public-values-only and rotate keys in the Supabase dashboard.
#
# URL RULES: production URLs must use HTTPS. Plain HTTP is accepted only for
# local development hosts (localhost, *.localhost, 127.0.0.1, [::1]); other
# HTTP hosts are rejected. URLs embedding a username/password are rejected.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR-PUBLISHABLE-ANON-KEY

# Password-reset redirect — required ONLY when VITE_APP_MODE=production.
#
# The exact absolute http(s) URL the emailed reset link returns the user to,
# e.g. https://your-app-origin/auth/reset-callback. It MUST also be registered
# in the Supabase dashboard (Auth → URL Configuration → Redirect URLs) —
# Supabase rejects un-registered redirects server-side. If this variable is
# unset or blank, the production app reports a clear configuration error
# (errResetRedirect) instead of inventing an origin. Keep the endpoint OUT of
# the browser bundle otherwise: it is only read at build time with the other
# VITE_* values. For the eventual ATCO handover, re-register this entry
# against the production origin in the ATCO project's dashboard.
VITE_AUTH_RESET_REDIRECT_URL=https://YOUR-APP-ORIGIN/auth/reset-callback
